    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=SCT378": {
      "title": "Head of School of Computer Science and Engineering",
      "description": "SCT378 Head of School of Computer Science and Engineering - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register More ▼ Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ More ▼ Head of School of Computer Science and Engineering Job Details: Job Description Middlesex University is an ambitious and progressive institution committed to empowering students and providing them with an educational experience that sets them up for success in life and work as we embark upon our 2031 University Strategy. Our triple intensity approach is focussed on Education, Research & Knowledge Exchange and Engagement. Based in North London and building on a proud history, our vision is to be a truly 21st century Global University. The University has over 38,000 students studying in London and at campuses in Dubai and Mauritius and over 274,000 alumni. The University’s diversity of experience and vibrancy are signature strengths that underpin all we do. Middlesex University London is seeking a visionary Head of School for the School of Computer Science and Engineering to lead and deliver an outstanding education and student experience as well as support research and knowledge exchange, innovation. The new Head of School will help shape and support the strategic direction of the Faculty of Science and Technology. Applicants should hold a PhD, possess an academic leadership background in education and student experience and would welcome applications from those who are experienced in developing industry partnerships and knowledge exchange activities. The new School of Computer Science and Engineering is part a large and vibrant faculty encompassing four new schools: Computer Science and Engineering, Sport, Environment and Health Sciences; Psychology and Neuroscience: and School of Biomedical and Pharmaceutical Sciences. The new Head of School will form part of a Senior Leadership team driven to implement and realise the emerging vision of the Department and Faculty where student educational achievement and work readiness is integral to that. The postholder will work with other Heads of School in the Faculty, two Deputy Deans, a Faculty Manager and the Dean to provide leadership and management in shaping the future of the Faculty. This is an exciting time to be joining Middlesex with a strong leadership, clarity of focus and a determination to deliver positive change across the University. The Faculty of Science and Technology is well placed with a refreshed portfolio of educational programmes, significant industry connections, strong research base and a dedicated team of academic, technical, and professional services staff. The appointment will be made on a permanent senior manager contract and depending on their experience could be made at Professorial level. Ultimately, we are looking for a leader who wants to contribute actively to the success of the faculty and has a vision for Computer Science and Engineering at Middlesex University. Applicants will be expected to demonstrate strong evidence of vision, innovation, leadership and managing academic staff in addition to a commitment to fostering and developing a collegial and collaborative academic environment within a school that encourages our students and academic staff to flourish. Informal enquiries should be made to Professor Klaus Dodds, Dean of Faculty, via email on K.dodds@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Faculty of Science & Technology Company Middlesex University Location Hendon Starting Salary Competitive Grade Senior Staff Contract Type Permanent FTE 1 Date Posted Friday 07 August 2026 Closing Date Sunday 27 September 2026 Reference SCT378 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=BAL48": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Strategy and International Business",
      "description": "BAL48 Senior Lecturer in Strategy and International Business - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register More ▼ Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ More ▼ Senior Lecturer in Strategy and International Business Job Details: Job Description Middlesex University is an ambitious and progressive institution committed to empowering students and providing them with an educational experience that sets them up for success in life and work as we embark upon our refreshed 2031 University Strategy. As we become an anchor University in North London we are building on our proud history and release our vision to be a truly 21st century Global University. The University has over 38,000 students studying in London and at campuses in Dubai and Mauritius and over 274,000 alumni. The University’s diversity of experience and vibrancy are signature strengths that underpin all we do. The Department of Strategy, Leadership and Operations at Middlesex University is seeking an enthusiastic Senior Lecturer to join our academic community on a teaching and research path. You will take an active lead role in teaching on a range of our programmes in the department, which have been refocussed and built our practice leading education agenda as we move forward with our AACSB accreditation journey. The ideal candidate will have expertise and a track record of research outputs in strategy and international business, with the flexibility to contribute to teaching across the department when required. In line with our vision to transform the lives of individual students and the futures of the communities in which we are embedded, we are looking for a candidate who excels in delivering high-quality, inclusive, and practice-led teaching. You will play a key role in shaping our students’ futures by delivering innovative and impactful teaching, fostering an engaging learning environment, and supporting student success at all levels of study. Your teaching will integrate real-world insights and address contemporary challenges, preparing students to become self-confident, employable, and responsible global citizens. You are expected to maintain a research profile, including outputs, normally of high international standing, and demonstrate commitment to making an impact on society, based on research and knowledge transfer. This is an exciting time to be joining Middlesex with strong leadership, clarity of focus and a determination to deliver positive change across the University. The Faculty of Business and Law is well placed, ranked #1 in Impact in Ref21, a refreshing suite of programmes, significant industry connections, and a dedicated team of staff. If you wish to discuss the job in further detail, please contact Professor & HoD, Strategy, Leadership and Operations, Professor Goudarz Azar at G.Azar@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Faculty of Business & Law Company Middlesex University Location Hendon Starting Salary £51,569\n            per annum Grade Grade 8 Contract Type Permanent FTE 1 Date Posted Tuesday 25 August 2026 Closing Date Friday 11 September 2026 Reference BAL48 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=ESE52": {
      "title": "Pre-Sessional and In-Sessional Academic Advisor",
      "description": "ESE52 Pre-Sessional and In-Sessional Academic Advisor - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register More ▼ Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ More ▼ Pre-Sessional and In-Sessional Academic Advisor Job Details: Job Description We are looking for a passionate and experienced Pre-Sessional and In-Sessional Academic Advisor to support the success of our international student community through the delivery of high-quality pre-sessional and in-sessional academic development programmes. This is an exciting opportunity to design and deliver engaging teaching, workshops, and one-to-one academic support that supports students develop the academic literacies, skills, and confidence needed to thrive in UK higher education. Working collaboratively across the University, you will contribute to curriculum development, student transitions, academic success initiatives, and the enhancement of the overall student experience. The successful candidate will have experience teaching English for Academic Purposes (EAP), academic skills, or related provision within a higher education environment, together with excellent interpersonal and communication skills. You will be confident supporting diverse student cohorts, developing inclusive learning resources, and using evidence and data to enhance student outcomes. You will be committed to innovative, student-centred practice and keen to contribute to scholarship, professional development, and cross-university partnerships that support international student success. For further information about the role please contact Annie Jennings, Director of Student Life, via email at A.Jennings@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Education & Student Experience Company Middlesex University Location Hendon Starting Salary £43,811\n            per annum Grade Grade 7 Contract Type Permanent Hours per Week 35.5 Date Posted Monday 24 August 2026 Closing Date Sunday 06 September 2026 Reference ESE52 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=ESE48": {
      "title": "Pre-Sessional and In-Sessional Academic Manager",
      "description": "ESE48 Pre-Sessional and In-Sessional Academic Manager - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register More ▼ Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ More ▼ Pre-Sessional and In-Sessional Academic Manager Job Details: Job Description We are seeking an experienced and dynamic Academic Manager to lead our Pre-Sessional English (PSE) and In-Sessional English for Academic Purposes (EAP) provision for international students. You will be responsible for the strategic leadership, design, delivery, quality assurance, and continuous enhancement of programmes that support students' successful progression into and through higher education. Managing academic staff, curriculum development, budgets, and operational delivery, you will ensure an outstanding learning experience across on-campus, hybrid, and online provision. The successful candidate will have significant experience of leading EAP provision within UK Higher Education, a strong understanding of UKVI and quality assurance requirements, and a proven track record of curriculum innovation, team leadership, and student-centred practice. For further information about the role please contact Annie Jennings, Director of Student Life, via email at A.Jennings@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Education & Student Experience Company Middlesex University Location Hendon Starting Salary £51,569\n            per annum Grade Grade 8 Contract Type Permanent FTE 1 Date Posted Friday 21 August 2026 Closing Date Sunday 06 September 2026 Reference ESE48 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
    },
